<urn:atm:triage:finding/AI11-QA5-ATM-QA-002-DELETION-GATE-TEST>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AI11-QA5-ATM-QA-002-DELETION-GATE-TEST" ;
  triage:title "Missing deletion-gate AST/dependency scan test" ;
  triage:description "AI.11 sprint doc requires a deletion-gate AST/dependency scan test verifying deleted UDS-transport code paths cannot be silently reintroduced. This test was never implemented. Should follow the same style as existing AST-based tests in crates/atm-architecture/tests/boundary_enforcement.rs." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-AI" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "QA" ;
  triage:severity "important" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "file_only" ;
  triage:status "disputed" ;
  triage:dispatchReady false ;
  triage:resolution "Fixed on feature/pAI-s11-post-merge-remediation, commit 472a9225 (test(ai11): add Windows transport deletion gate, crates/atm-architecture/tests/boundary_enforcement.rs)." ;
  triage:notes "DISPUTED, not a confirmed false closure -- QA-6's absence claim appears to be a stale-worktree artifact, not an actual missing test. quality-mgr's QA-6 pass (PR #607 comment https://github.com/randlee/atm-core/pull/607#issuecomment-5050680007) reported, via full-file read + workspace-wide grep of 'the commit under review, 472a9225', zero matches for named_pipe/AF_UNIX/deletion_gate/etc. and a 764-line file. Direct re-verification (team-lead, 2026-07-22) of commit 472a9225 itself (git show 472a9225:crates/atm-architecture/tests/boundary_enforcement.rs) shows the commit DOES add the required test: const AI11_RETIRED_WINDOWS_TRANSPORT_SYMBOLS list plus fn ai11_deletion_gate_preserves_windows_loopback_transport_boundary() and fn ai11_deletion_gate_detector_rejects_retired_windows_transport_fixture(), 859 lines total, covering all six sprint-doc Required-Tests-table items (pipe, AF_UNIX, generic frame codec, duplicate router, non-loopback bind, adapter storage/nudge calls). PR #607's headRefOid is confirmed 472a9225 via `gh pr view 607`. Critically: the local worktree at /Users/randlee/Documents/github/atm-core-worktrees/feature/pAI-s11-post-merge-remediation was found (before a fresh `git pull`) sitting one commit BEHIND origin, at 8a7ea589 (763 lines, no deletion-gate test) -- an exact byte-for-byte match to QA-6's reported '764 lines' / zero-match state. This strongly suggests QA-6's reviewer subagents read that same un-pulled local worktree rather than the actual commit 472a9225 content, i.e. a worktree-fetch hygiene bug in the QA pipeline, not a false-closure by the triage record. Status set to 'disputed' pending: (1) re-running QA-6 against a freshly-pulled worktree, (2) confirming with quality-mgr which path/commit its subagents actually read. Do NOT dispatch new deletion-gate test work based on this finding without first re-verifying against a freshly pulled worktree -- the test may already satisfy the requirement. Flagging to team-lead/user for adjudication; not unilaterally closing or reopening." ;
  triage:openOn <urn:atm:triage:worktree/s11/8a7ea589> ;
  triage:promoteTo <urn:atm:triage:worktree/s11/8a7ea589> ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-07-22T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime .

